      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Corinna Schleiffer",
      "description": "Northburgh Castle. Castle ruins in Greencastle, Inishowen, Co. Donegal, Rep. of Ireland.\n\"The Annals of Ulster Clonmacnois both confirm that the Norman, Richard de Burgh, Red Earl of Ulster, constructed Northburgh Castle in 1305. At the time the de Burgh controlled most of Ireland, however, Inishowen and Tir Connail escaped his grasp.The O'Donnells and the O'Doherty's remained free and independent here, largely due to the aid they received from the old Norse kingdom of Argyle and the Hebrides.\" (From an info board at the castle entrance)",
      "dateCreated": "2004-07-28",
      "categories": [
        "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
        "Greencastle Castle, County Donegal",
        "Images by Corinna Schleiffer",
        "Images from Geograph Britain and Ireland",
        "Images from Geograph Britain and Ireland needing category review",
